From 7a0709264bcf753b312882fc1ebfd93a62730e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cylewitruk <cyle.witruk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Carry a connection without finalizing it, and tell the
 verifier more about a prefix

A carried connection no longer runs the TLS client's finalization when
it ends: the verifier is told the connection is over and the proof state
is dropped unused. The verifier had stopped taking part, so the prover
alone advanced state the session shares.

A tap can tell whether application data was sent beyond a prefix, which
the alert answering a server's close is not, and a prefix tells how much
of what it received had begun to arrive before the last of what it sent
was forwarded.
